# REC in HOME, stopped: a bar's count-in, then two keys recorded into the
# take; REC again ends it before the next bar, and PLAY/STOP stops.
--button 0.10:REC
--key 1.30:7:100:0.15
--key 1.55:11:90:0.15
--button 2.05:REC
--button 2.30:PLAY/STOP
# SEQ, REC held: step record from step 1 (the clip has a bar, so the head
# wraps): a key; a chord of two tied into the next step with A#3; a rest; a
# note at MIDI IN. Then REC let go.
--button 2.40:SEQ
--button 2.50:REC:0.95
--key 2.60:16:100:0.08
--key 2.75:7:90:0.2
--key 2.76:11:80:0.19
--key 2.85:5:100:0.03
--key 3.05:5:100:0.03
--note 3.15:63:70:0.1
# HOME, PLAY/STOP, and three keys while playing; SHIFT + REC captures them
# where they were heard. Two more passes of the bar.
--button 3.50:HOME
--button 3.55:PLAY/STOP
--key 3.70:9:100:0.1
--key 3.90:12:90:0.1
--key 4.10:14:80:0.1
--button 4.30:SEL:0.1
--button 4.35:REC
